<main class="container">

    <!-- 1. CONCEPTS (Slate) -->
    <section id="concepts" class="card theme-slate">
        <div class="card-header">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-database"></i> Core Concepts
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
            <div class="grid-2">
                <div>
                    <h3>Persistence</h3>
                    <p>When a program closes, variables in RAM are lost. <strong>Files</strong> provide persistence, allowing data to be saved (written) and reloaded (read) later.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3>File & Buffers</h3>
                    <p>A <strong>Text File</strong> is a sequence of characters structured in lines. A <strong>Buffer</strong> is a temporary memory area used to move data between the program and the file system.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3>File Modes</h3>
            <div class="table-responsive">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Mode</th>
                            <th>Description</th>
                            <th>Behavior if file exists</th>
                            <th>Behavior if file doesn't exist</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>'r'</code></td>
                            <td><strong>Read</strong></td>
                            <td>Reads from start.</td>
                            <td style="color: red;">Error (File Not Found)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>'w'</code></td>
                            <td><strong>Write</strong></td>
                            <td style="color: red;">OVERWRITES (deletes content).</td>
                            <td>Creates new file.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><code>'a'</code></td>
                            <td><strong>Append</strong></td>
                            <td>Adds to end.</td>
                            <td>Creates new file.</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. READING (Sky) -->
    <section id="reading" class="card theme-sky">
        <div class="card-header">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-glasses"></i> Reading Files
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
            <p class="mb-4">Using the <code>with open()</code> statement is best practice. It automatically closes the file, preventing resource leaks.</p>

            <div class="grid-2">
                <div>
                    <h3>Line by Line (Preferred)</h3>
                    <pre><code class="python"># Efficient for big files
with open("data.txt", "r") as f:
    for line in f:
        print(line.strip())</code></pre>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3>Read All Lines</h3>
                    <pre><code class="python"># Loads entire file into a list
with open("data.txt", "r") as f:
    lines = f.readlines()
    
# Process list
print(lines[0]) </code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="tip-box">
                <span class="tip-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> The newline character</span>
                <p>Lines in a file end with <code>\n</code>. Use <code>.strip()</code> to remove it when reading strings.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. WRITING (Emerald) -->
    <section id="writing" class="card theme-emerald">
        <div class="card-header">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-pen-nib"></i> Writing & Appending
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
            <div class="grid-2">
                <div>
                    <h3>Writing (Overwriting)</h3>
                    <pre><code class="python"># CAUTION: Deletes old content!
with open("output.txt", "w") as f:
    f.write("First Line\n")
    f.write("Second Line\n")</code></pre>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3>Appending</h3>
                    <pre><code class="python"># Safe: Add to end
with open("log.txt", "a") as f:
    f.write("New Log Entry\n")</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 4. PARALLEL ARRAYS (Rose) -->
    <section id="parallel" class="card theme-rose">
        <div class="card-header">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-table"></i> Processing Parallel Arrays
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
            <p class="mb-4">Often data is stored in separate files (e.g., <code>names.txt</code> and <code>scores.txt</code>) or columns that relate to each other by index.</p>

            <h3>Scenario: Loading Sales Data</h3>
            <pre><code class="python">names = []
sales = []

# Assuming a CSV format: "Name,Sales"
with open("sales_data.txt", "r") as file:
    for line in file:
        parts = line.strip().split(",")
        names.append(parts[0])
        sales.append(int(parts[1]))

# Now we can process them together
for i in range(len(names)):
    print(f"{names[i]} sold {sales[i]} units")</code></pre>

            <h3>Scenario: Finding the Top Seller</h3>
            <pre><code class="python">max_sales = -1
winner_index = -1

for i in range(len(sales)):
    if sales[i] > max_sales:
        max_sales = sales[i]
        winner_index = i

print(f"Winner: {names[winner_index]}")</code></pre>
        </div>
    </section>

